    "result_text": "The build is green: **BUILD SUCCESS**, all 68 tests pass (0 failures, 0 errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**What `memberId` is:** `REGION` (postcode range \u2192 city table \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) + `FY` (2-digit fiscal year of the registrationDate, same year segment as `fiscalYear`) + `HASH8` (first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` \u2014 the same HASH8 as the region-and-hash identity) + `CHK` (single Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n- **`Owner` entity** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode` field/column (`customer_code`) with `memberId` (`member_id`) and its accessors.\n- **DB schema** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 renamed the column to `member_id` (widened to 32 to fit the `UNKNOWN` region case plus a collision suffix).\n- **`CustomerCode` \u2192 `MemberId`** (new class, old deleted) \u2014 now builds the full `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, computing FY via the mapper's single `fiscalYearEnding` definition and CHK via Luhn.\n- **`AssignCustomerCode` \u2192 `AssignMemberId`** (new class, old deleted) \u2014 collision de-duplication now applies to `memberId` (`-<n>` suffix), and it reads the registrationDate (already resolved upstream) to compute FY.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 dropped the `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings/methods; `memberId` now auto-maps from the entity; `locality` derives its region directly from postcode/city (the same region embedded in `memberId`); reverse-mapping ignore updated to `memberId`.\n- **Audit** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated` human-readable line now logs `memberId` (dropping `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`); `OwnerCreatedEvent`'s identifier field is renamed to `memberId` and carries it.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 the `assignCustomerCode` step became `assignMemberId` with updated wiring/comments.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single `memberId` property (the generated `OwnerDto` follows), so the removed fields no longer appear in responses.\n\nThe acceptance tests confirm the behaviour: `memberId` starts with the pinned region and contains the computed HASH8 (Cp56/Cp32), distinct owners get distinct memberIds (Cp41), `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` are absent (Cp09/16/14/31), and the audit line/event reference `memberId` (Cp21/43/53).",
